WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.537
Two design choices protect the evidence.

2
00:00:02.537 --> 00:00:05.400
First, no names reach the issue tracker.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.634
Issue titles come from a fixed catalog,
bodies carry object IDs and fingerprints,

4
00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:14.462
and a test checks that no name
from either run slips through.

5
00:00:14.462 --> 00:00:17.438
Names stay in the
access-controlled evidence store.

6
00:00:17.438 --> 00:00:21.274
Second, each package records
the hash of the one before it,

7
00:00:21.274 --> 00:00:23.151
so the packages form a chain.

8
00:00:23.151 --> 00:00:27.150
Replace a package, or skip a day,
and the chain breaks visibly.

9
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.033
There's no signature; the hashes
plus storage that can't be

10
00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:35.470
edited or deleted do that job, and
signing stays the ISSO's choice.
